chapter.v:
	‘Take from 

	 among you an offering to the Lord. Whoever is of a willing heart, let him bring it as an offering to the Lord: gold, silver, and bronze;
 [Ex. 25:2; 1 Chr. 29:14; Mark 12:41- 44; 2 Cor. 8:10-12; 9:7 g Ex. 38:24]

	blue, purple, 

	 and scarlet thread, fine linen, and goats’ hair;
 [Ex. 36:8 i Ex.]

	oil for 

	 the light, and spices for the anointing oil and for the sweet incense;
 [Ex. 25:6;]

	the tabernacle, 

	 its tent, its covering, its clasps, its boards, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets;
 [Ex. 26:1, 2;]

	the ark 

	 and its poles, with the mercy seat, and the veil of the covering;
 [Ex. 25:10-22]

	the table 

	 and its poles, all its utensils, and the showbread;
 [Ex. 25:30; Lev.] [Ex. 25:23]

	also the 

	 lampstand for the light, its utensils, its lamps, and the oil for the light;
 [Ex. 25:31]

	the incense 

	 altar, its poles, the anointing oil, the sweet incense, and the screen for the door at the entrance of the tabernacle;
 [Ex. 30:25 s Ex.] [Ex. 30:1]

	the altar 

	 of burnt offering with its bronze grating, its poles, all its utensils, and the laver and its base;
 [Ex. 27:1-8]

	the hangings 

	 of the court, its pillars, their sockets, and the screen for the gate of the court;
 [Ex. 27:9-18]

	And Moses 

	 said to the children of Israel, “See, the Lord has called by name Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah;
 [Ex. 31:1-6]
